      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Ellisen.",
        "AbstractText": "In this issue of JEM, Sundaram et al. (https://doi.org/10.1084/jem.20170354) report a mechanism by which the normal epithelial wound healing response is \"hijacked\" to promote invasion and metastasis in head and neck squamous carcinomas (HNSCCs), a finding that unveils new markers of poor outcomes and potential targets for therapeutic intervention."
